     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there! <div><br></div><div>I was wondering if it is at all possible to view all the p-values associated with the logistic regression aside from just the main exposure? I am interested in seeing if some of the covariates in my model were significantly associated with the methylation levels as well for QC. </div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks! <br><div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><a name=\"m_-7692168974963818625_SignatureSanitizer_SafeHtmlFilter_UNIQUE_ID_SafeHtmlFilter__MailAutoSig\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:black\">Laetitia Meyrueix<br></span></a><span style=\"color:black;font-size:12.8px\">Doctoral Student, Department of Nutrition<br></span><span style=\"color:black;font-size:12.8px\">Gillings School of Global Public Health<br></span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font color=\"#000000\">University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill<br></font></span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/lmeyrueix4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/lmeyrueix4&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230991888000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2oyerWhs3xQWSCAtJL6N4G\">Twitter</a><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"> | </span><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/laetitiameyrueix/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.linkedin.com/in/laetitiameyrueix/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230991888000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3E7EyyEQ27WXBCUq1ggat_\">LinkedIn</a><br><i style=\"font-size:12.8px\">preferred pronouns: she, her, hers</i></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><br><div>\r\n        <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n            <tbody><tr>\r\n             